IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sa-messages`

-- Spam Act 2003 (Cth), ss 5, 6, 7, 16, 17, 18, 25, Schedules 1, 2 and 3 cl 5 -- worked cases from the seat of the consumer
-- receiving marketing messages (and, for s 25 and Sch 3, the sender).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, an ACMA decision or the Spam Regulations 2021 (not deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_spam-act-2003_baseline.py). Expected results
-- were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe): in July 2024 Chloe, 21, gets marketing calls
-- and texts and asks "Can she stop them?" (c044). The scenario names no sender, no consent and no dates; the senders, the
-- ticked box and the STOP reply are the encoder's. Fixtures not marked (c044) are invented for the case. No Daniel event
-- cites this Act; the sender-side penalty cases are invented (a company like his, Jarrah).

§ `Fixtures`

`a telemarketing voice call to Chloe's mobile on a standard telephone service (c044)` MEANS Message WITH
