§ `ss 5, 6, 7 -- commercial electronic message, Australian link`

-- c044: the calls are voice calls on a standard telephone service (s 5(5)); the texts are electronic messages.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this an electronic message` `a telemarketing voice call to Chloe's mobile on a standard telephone service (c044)`)
#ASSERT `Is this an electronic message` `a retailer's promotional text to Chloe naming itself, with a reply-STOP line (c044)`

#ASSERT `Is this a commercial electronic message` `a retailer's promotional text to Chloe naming itself, with a reply-STOP line (c044)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this a commercial electronic message` `a friend's text with no commercial purpose`)

#ASSERT `Does it have an Australian link` `a text from overseas claiming a parcel fee, meant to get her card details by deception`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does it have an Australian link` `an overseas shop's email read by Chloe abroad on a foreign device`)

§ `Schedule 1 -- designated messages`

#ASSERT `Is it a designated commercial electronic message` `her bank's text that her statement is ready, with its name and logo`
#ASSERT `Is it a designated commercial electronic message` `a registered charity's email selling its own raffle tickets, with no contact details`
#ASSERT `Is it a designated commercial electronic message` `Chloe's own university's email offering a short course it runs`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it a designated commercial electronic message` `another university's email offering a course, Chloe never enrolled there`)

§ `Schedule 2 -- consent and withdrawal`

#ASSERT NOT (`Has my unsubscribe taken effect` 4)
#ASSERT `Has my unsubscribe taken effect` 5

#ASSERT `Did I consent to this message` `Chloe ticked a box to receive the retailer's offers (c044)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I consent to this message` `Chloe never dealt with the sender (c044)`)
#ASSERT `Did I consent to this message` `Chloe ticked the box, then replied STOP; 2 business days completed (c044)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I consent to this message` `Chloe ticked the box, then replied STOP; 5 business days completed (c044)`)
#ASSERT `Did I consent to this message` `an existing customer, consent reasonably inferred from her conduct`
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I consent to this message` `her number merely published online, nothing more`)
#ASSERT `Did I consent to this message` `her work email conspicuously published, message relevant to her job`

-- c044: Chloe replies STOP on a Monday; with no public holiday the retailer may rely on her consent to Friday.
#ASSERT (`How many calendar days until my unsubscribe takes effect` Monday) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT (`How many calendar days until my unsubscribe takes effect` Wednesday) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT (`How many calendar days until my unsubscribe takes effect` Sunday) EQUALS 6

§ `s 16 -- did the sender need my consent (c044: can she stop them?)`

#ASSERT (`Did the sender need my consent` `a telemarketing voice call to Chloe's mobile on a standard telephone service (c044)` `Chloe never dealt with the sender (c044)`) EQUALS `the Spam Act does not reach it, because it is not an electronic message`
#ASSERT (`Did the sender need my consent` `a friend's text with no commercial purpose` `Chloe never dealt with the sender (c044)`) EQUALS `no consent needed, because it is not a commercial electronic message`
#ASSERT (`Did the sender need my consent` `an overseas shop's email read by Chloe abroad on a foreign device` `Chloe never dealt with the sender (c044)`) EQUALS `no consent needed, because it has no Australian link`
#ASSERT (`Did the sender need my consent` `Chloe's own university's email offering a short course it runs` `Chloe never dealt with the sender (c044)`) EQUALS `no consent needed, because it is a designated commercial electronic message`
#ASSERT (`Did the sender need my consent` `a retailer's promotional text to Chloe naming itself, with a reply-STOP line (c044)` `Chloe ticked the box, then replied STOP; 2 business days completed (c044)`) EQUALS `it was allowed, because I consented`
#ASSERT (`Did the sender need my consent` `a retailer's promotional text to Chloe naming itself, with a reply-STOP line (c044)` `Chloe ticked the box, then replied STOP; 5 business days completed (c044)`) EQUALS `it breaks s 16(1), unless the sender shows it was sent by mistake or it could not have known of the Australian link`
#ASSERT (`Did the sender need my consent` `a retailer's promotional text to Chloe naming itself, with a reply-STOP line (c044)` `Chloe never dealt with the sender (c044)`) EQUALS `it breaks s 16(1), unless the sender shows it was sent by mistake or it could not have known of the Australian link`

§ `s 17 -- sender information`

#ASSERT `Must it identify the sender` `her bank's text that her statement is ready, with its name and logo`
#ASSERT NOT (`Must it identify the sender` `a friend's text with no commercial purpose`)

-- c044: the bare text breaks s 17; a designated charity message with no contact details breaks it too.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does it break the sender-information rule` `a retailer's promotional text to Chloe naming itself, with a reply-STOP line (c044)`)
#ASSERT `Does it break the sender-information rule` `a promotional text to Chloe naming no sender and offering no way to unsubscribe (c044)`
#ASSERT `Does it break the sender-information rule` `a registered charity's email selling its own raffle tickets, with no contact details`

§ `s 18 -- unsubscribe facility`

#ASSERT `Must it let me unsubscribe` `a retailer's promotional text to Chloe naming itself, with a reply-STOP line (c044)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Must it let me unsubscribe` `her bank's text that her statement is ready, with its name and logo`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must it let me unsubscribe` `a gym's promotional text under a membership contract inconsistent with an unsubscribe facility`)

#ASSERT `Does it break the unsubscribe rule` `a promotional text to Chloe naming no sender and offering no way to unsubscribe (c044)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does it break the unsubscribe rule` `a registered charity's email selling its own raffle tickets, with no contact details`)

§ `s 25 and Schedule 3 -- what a sender can be made to pay, in penalty units`

-- A company like Daniel's Jarrah (a body corporate), invented: no Spam Act event in the plan.
#ASSERT (`What is the most I can be made to pay per contravention` `s 16, unsolicited messages` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`What is the most I can be made to pay per contravention` `s 18, unsubscribe facility` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 50

#ASSERT (`What is the most I can be made to pay for one day` `s 16, unsolicited messages` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 10000

#ASSERT (`How many penalty units is the infringement notice` `s 16, unsolicited messages` TRUE 1) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`How many penalty units is the infringement notice` `s 16, unsolicited messages` TRUE 300) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`How many penalty units is the infringement notice` `s 17, sender information` FALSE 49) EQUALS 98

